==Battleground==
*1 [[Queen B]] spawns as the boss after 7.4 seconds<sup>222f</sup>.
*1 [[THE SLOTH]] spawns after 22.2 seconds<sup>666f</sup>.
*30 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 29.6 seconds<sup>888f</sup>, delay 7.4~14.8 seconds<sup>222f~444f</sup>.
*5 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 44.4 seconds<sup>1,332f</sup>, delay 1.47~2.93 seconds<sup>44f~88f</sup>.
*4 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 111.07 seconds<sup>3,332f</sup>, delay 2.2~4.4 seconds<sup>66f~132f</sup>.
*3 [[Brollow]]s spawn after 177.73 seconds<sup>5,332f</sup>, delay 2.93~5.87 seconds<sup>88f~176f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 222.2 seconds<sup>6,666f</sup>, delay 29.6~37 seconds<sup>888f~1,110f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn after 229.6 seconds<sup>6,888f</sup>, delay 29.6~37 seconds<sup>888f~1,110f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Courier Cat]] breaks both this stage and [[Bombergirl (Deadly) (Queen & Maiden)|Bombergirl]]. Make sure to bring both a [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red]] [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|Crowd-Controller unit]] like [[iCat]] and a secondary [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attacker]] like [[Medalist Cat]], and you should be fine for Bakoo.

For Honey Trap specifically, simple meatshielding using units like [[Crazed Macho Cat]] and [[Catellite]] alongside something fast to clear Brollows like [[Butterfly Cat]] should be enough.

==Trivia==
*A "honey trap" is a strategem which involves using an attractive person to lure the victim into a false relationship, matching [[Queen B]]'s theme of lust as one of the seven deadly sins.
*The enemy base's HP is fully composed of 7s, which are believed to be lucky in many cultures.

